      "description": "Watch Standard Liege vs Lommel United highlights and goals from Jupiler Pro League on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 24, 2026. The Jupiler Pro League season continued with a high-stakes encounter as Standard Liege hosted Lommel United . Both teams entered the pitch on August 24, 2026, determined to claim a vital victory in front of a passionate crowd. A Tactical Stalemate in the Opening Half The first half was characterized by defensive discipline and tactical awareness from both sides. Standard Liege sought to dictate the tempo, but Lommel United remained compact, closing down spaces effectively. The physical nature of the contest became apparent in the 34th minute when Yllan Okou received the game's first yellow card for a late challenge. Despite several promising build-ups, clear-cut chances were at a premium, and the referee blew for half-time with the scoreline still level. Drammeh’s Explosive Introduction The second half began with immediate intensity as Alexis Trouillet picked up a yellow card just a minute after the restart. The match reached its turning point in the 62nd minute when Salieu Drammeh was introduced as a substitute for Dennis Eckert . This proved to be a masterstroke by the coaching staff. In the 68th minute, Bernard Nguene delivered a perfectly weighted pass to Drammeh , who clinicaly finished to break the deadlock and make it 1-0. Sensing blood, Standard Liege struck again almost immediately. In the 73rd minute, the red-hot Salieu Drammeh found the back of the net for the second time in five minutes, doubling the lead and leaving the visitors stunned. His clinical finishing completely altered the momentum of the game, providing the hosts with a comfortable cushion heading into the final stages. Late Drama and the Final Whistle As the clock ticked down, Lommel United struggled to find a way back into the contest despite a flurry of tactical substitutions. Their frustrations boiled over in stoppage time when Yllan Okou received his second yellow card in the 91st minute, resulting in a red card. With a man advantage and a two-goal lead, Standard Liege comfortably saw out the remaining minutes to secure all three points, leaving their fans celebrating a dominant second-half performance."
